window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-a7459570776840aa"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"browser-extension\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"chatgpt\">ChatGPT 浏览器扩展</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取对应 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，你可以使用 ChatGPT 浏览器扩展，通过 Google Chrome、Microsoft Edge、Brave、Opera 或 Vivaldi 进行操作。ChatGPT 可以读取或操作你已经登录的网站，例如 LinkedIn、Salesforce、Gmail 或内部工具。</p> <p>这五种浏览器都支持在标签页中 @ 提及以及由桌面应用控制浏览器。Chrome、Edge、Brave 和 Vivaldi 还支持侧边栏聊天。<strong>Opera 不支持侧边栏聊天</strong>；请在桌面应用中启动相关任务。</p> <p>设置其他浏览器前，请先更新 ChatGPT 桌面应用。浏览器是否可用还取决于功能的逐步推出状态和工作区设置。</p> <p>如果想让 ChatGPT 控制内置浏览器，可使用 <code>@Browser</code>。<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001277-using-the-built-in-browser-in-the-chatgpt-desktop-app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">内置浏览器（需联网）</a>支持登录，并会在 ChatGPT 内完成浏览，不使用你的常规浏览器配置档案。</p> <p>ChatGPT 也会根据任务需要切换工具：有专用集成时使用插件；需要已登录的浏览器上下文时使用你的浏览器；访问 localhost 时则使用内置浏览器。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>提示（<code>warning</code>）</strong>: 请将页面内容视为不可信上下文；允许 ChatGPT 继续前，请先检查网站。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-chatgpt-from-chrome\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"use-side-chat-in-your-browser\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt_1\">在浏览器侧边栏中使用 ChatGPT</h2> <p>Chrome、Edge、Brave 和 Vivaldi 支持侧边栏聊天。</p> <p>在当前页面旁打开 ChatGPT，询问页面相关问题，或继续开展可结合页面上下文、本地文件和已连接应用的任务。任务需要时，ChatGPT 可以使用你已打开的标签页作为上下文。</p> <ol> <li>打开你想处理的网页。</li> <li>在浏览器工具栏或 <strong>Extensions（扩展程序）</strong> 菜单中选择 ChatGPT。在 macOS 上，也可以按下 <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>.</kbd>。</li> <li>就当前网页提出问题或交代任务。</li> </ol> <p>侧边栏面板会留在你打开它的那个标签页中。你在侧边栏中开始的聊天也会出现在 ChatGPT 应用里；你也可以在侧边栏中打开最近的 ChatGPT 聊天，从而在两个界面之间继续工作。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：在当前 Chrome 标签页旁打开的 ChatGPT。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"bring-tabs-and-selected-text-into-a-chat\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">将标签页和选中文本带入聊天</h2> <p>如果希望桌面应用把某个网页用作上下文，可以在桌面应用中提及已打开的浏览器标签页。支持侧边栏聊天的浏览器也允许你在侧边栏中提及标签页，或选中网页上的文字并带入聊天，以便针对某段内容提问，而不必复制整页。</p> <p>在支持侧边栏聊天的浏览器中，你还可以右键单击页面并选择 <strong>Ask ChatGPT（询问 ChatGPT）</strong>。侧边栏会带上相关页面上下文打开，你可以直接在浏览器中继续任务。</p> <p><a id=\"ask-about-a-youtube-video\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"youtube\">询问 YouTube 视频内容</h3> <p>打开 YouTube 视频，然后在受支持的侧边栏聊天中询问相关问题。如果视频提供字幕，ChatGPT 可以使用带时间戳的字幕稿来解释、总结或回答内容问题。</p> <p>请将网页内容、选中的文本和视频字幕稿都视为不可信上下文。让 ChatGPT 使用或操作这些信息前，请先检查页面和任何权限请求。</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-chrome-extension\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"set-up-your-browser\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">设置浏览器</h2> <p>在电脑上安装浏览器，然后在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中打开 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer Use（电脑操作）</strong>。如果主列表中没有显示你的浏览器，请展开 <strong>More browsers（更多浏览器）</strong>。</p> <ol> <li>选择浏览器，并按照提示安装所需插件。</li> <li>在该浏览器旁选择 <strong>Install（安装）</strong>，打开浏览器扩展商店页面。安装 ChatGPT 扩展并检查浏览器显示的权限请求。</li> <li>返回 <strong>Computer Use（电脑操作）</strong>，确认浏览器旁显示 <strong>Manage（管理）</strong>。</li> <li>开始一个 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 聊天，并通过 <code>@</code> 提及选择你的浏览器。请使用安装了该扩展的浏览器配置档案。</li> </ol> <p><strong>Computer Use（电脑操作）</strong> 中的浏览器开关决定该浏览器是否出现在 <code>@</code> 提及菜单中。选择 <strong>Manage（管理）</strong> 可以更改网站权限。</p> <blockquote> <p>插图：通过 Chrome 扩展连接 Google Chrome 的 Computer Use 设置。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-a-chrome-task-from-chatgpt\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"start-a-browser-task-from-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"chatgpt_2\">从 ChatGPT 启动浏览器任务</h2> <p>完成设置后，开始一个新的 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 聊天。在 <code>@</code> 提及菜单中选择 <strong>Chrome</strong>、<strong>Edge</strong>、<strong>Brave Browser</strong>、<strong>Opera</strong> 或 <strong>Vivaldi</strong>，指定 ChatGPT 使用哪个浏览器。例如：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Edge open Salesforce and update the account from these call notes.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">@Edge 打开 Salesforce，并根据这些通话记录更新该账户。</div></div> <p>你也可以提及一个已打开的标签页，为聊天提供该页面的上下文。Opera 虽然不支持侧边栏聊天，但支持这些桌面应用工作流。</p> <p><a id=\"control-website-access\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">控制网站访问权限</h2> <p>默认情况下，ChatGPT 每次与新网站交互前都会询问。提示会按照网站主机名显示，例如 <code>example.com</code>。</p> <p>当 ChatGPT 询问是否使用某个网站时，请根据任务和你能接受的风险选择合适选项：</p> <ul> <li><strong>Allow once（允许一次）</strong>：允许 ChatGPT 这次使用该网站。</li> <li><strong>Allow for this site（允许此网站）</strong>：允许 ChatGPT 以后再次使用该网站而不必询问。</li> <li><strong>Allow for all sites（允许所有网站）</strong>：允许 ChatGPT 使用网站而不再询问。</li> <li><strong>Decline（拒绝）</strong>：阻止 ChatGPT 使用该网站。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"manage-allowed-and-blocked-websites\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">管理允许和阻止的网站</h3> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，前往 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer Use（电脑操作）</strong>，然后选择浏览器旁的 <strong>Manage（管理）</strong>，管理域名允许列表和阻止列表。允许列表中的域名可供 ChatGPT 再次使用而无需询问；阻止列表中的域名则不允许使用。受支持的浏览器共用这些网站权限。</p> <p>从允许列表中删除域名，意味着 ChatGPT 下次会重新询问。从阻止列表中删除域名，意味着 ChatGPT 可以再次询问，而不是直接将该域名视为已阻止。</p> <p><a id=\"allow-for-all-sites\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_5\">允许访问所有网站</h4> <p>如果选择 <strong>Allow for all sites（允许所有网站）</strong>，ChatGPT 使用网站前就不再请求确认。只有在你信任 ChatGPT 使用浏览器中任意网站的情况下，才应选择此选项。</p> <p><a id=\"browser-history\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"_6\">浏览历史</h4> <p>浏览历史可能包含敏感遥测信息、内部 URL、搜索词，以及已登录设备上的浏览活动。如果允许 ChatGPT 访问浏览历史，相关记录可能成为 ChatGPT 执行任务时的上下文。恶意或误导性的网页内容可能增加 ChatGPT 将这些数据复制到非预期位置的风险。</p> <p>ChatGPT 想要使用浏览历史时会先询问。历史记录访问范围会限定在当前请求中，而且没有“始终允许”的选项。</p> <p><a id=\"data-and-security\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">数据与安全</h2> <p><a id=\"chrome-extension-permissions\"></a></p> <p><a id=\"browser-extension-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_8\">浏览器扩展权限</h3> <p>安装扩展时，浏览器会要求你接受相应权限。例如，Chrome 的权限提示可能包括：</p> <ul> <li>访问页面调试器</li> <li>读取和更改你在所有网站上的全部数据</li> <li>读取和更改你在所有已登录设备上的浏览历史</li> <li>显示通知</li> <li>读取和更改书签</li> <li>管理下载内容</li> <li>与配套的本机应用通信</li> <li>查看和管理标签页分组</li> </ul> <p>这些扩展权限使它能够执行浏览器工作流。ChatGPT 在使用网站或浏览历史前，仍会使用自己的确认、设置、允许列表和阻止列表。</p> <p><a id=\"memories\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">记忆</h3> <p>电脑操作遵循你的记忆设置。如果启用了记忆，ChatGPT 在浏览器中工作时可以使用相关的已保存记忆。如果关闭记忆，浏览器控制就不会使用记忆。</p> <p><a id=\"what-openai-stores-from-browsing\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"openai\">OpenAI 会保存哪些浏览活动</h3> <p>OpenAI 不会单独保存一份完整的浏览器扩展操作记录。只有当浏览活动成为 ChatGPT 上下文的一部分时，OpenAI 才会存储相关内容，例如 ChatGPT 从页面读取的文本、屏幕截图、工具调用、摘要、消息或其他聊天内容。</p> <p>ChatGPT 数据控制设置同样适用于在上下文中处理的内容。除非确有必要，而且你能逐项检查每个提示，否则请避免通过浏览器任务发送秘密或高度敏感的信息。</p> <p><a id=\"troubleshooting\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">故障排除</h2> <p>如果 ChatGPT 无法连接到浏览器，请先确认 ChatGPT 要访问的网站没有被列入 <strong>Settings（设置）</strong> 中的阻止列表。如果网站未被阻止，请按以下步骤检查：</p> <ol> <li>更新 ChatGPT 桌面应用。如果电脑上安装了多个 ChatGPT 或 Codex 桌面应用，请逐一更新，或移除不再使用的副本。</li> <li>重启浏览器。在 Chrome、Edge、Brave 或 Vivaldi 中，从工具栏或 <strong>Extensions（扩展程序）</strong> 菜单重新打开 ChatGPT，并确认侧边栏聊天已加载。Opera 不支持侧边栏聊天；请在桌面应用中检查连接。</li> <li>在 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer Use（电脑操作）</strong> 中确认浏览器已出现，并显示 <strong>Manage（管理）</strong>。如果仍显示 <strong>Install（安装）</strong>，请重新完成设置流程。如果浏览器没有出现在 <code>@</code> 提及菜单中，请打开它的开关。</li> <li>确认当前使用的浏览器配置档案就是安装扩展的那个配置档案。如果使用多个配置档案，请在当前配置档案中安装并启用扩展。</li> <li>开始新的 ChatGPT Work 或 Codex 聊天，然后重试浏览器任务。这有助于清除仅存在于当前聊天中的连接状态。</li> <li>重启 ChatGPT 桌面应用，然后重试。如果扩展仍无法连接，请通过 <strong>Settings（设置）&gt; Computer Use（电脑操作）</strong> 重新安装。</li> <li>如果 ChatGPT 仍无法使用浏览器，请在应用中运行 <code>/feedback</code>，并在联系支持团队时附上聊天 ID。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"upload-files\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">上传文件</h3> <p>如果 Chrome 任务需要从电脑上传文件，请允许 Chrome 扩展访问 Chrome 中的文件 URL：</p> <ol> <li>在 Chrome 中，选择工具栏里的扩展图标，然后单击 <strong>Manage Extensions（管理扩展程序）</strong>。</li> <li>在扩展卡片上单击 <strong>Details（详情）</strong>。</li> <li>打开 <strong>Allow access to file URLs（允许访问文件网址）</strong>。</li> </ol> <p>修改此设置后，请重新启动 ChatGPT 任务。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"browser-extension\">Browser extension</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>Use the ChatGPT browser extension to work in Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Brave, Opera, or Vivaldi from the ChatGPT desktop app. ChatGPT can read or act on sites where you're already signed in, such as LinkedIn, Salesforce, Gmail, or internal tools.</p> <p>All five browsers support tab mentions and browser control from the desktop app. Chrome, Edge, Brave, and Vivaldi also support side chat. <strong>Opera doesn't support side chat</strong>; start its tasks in the desktop app instead.</p> <p>Update the ChatGPT desktop app before setting up another browser. Browser availability can depend on rollout and your workspace settings.</p> <p>To let ChatGPT control its built-in browser instead, use <code>@Browser</code>. The <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001277-using-the-built-in-browser-in-the-chatgpt-desktop-app\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">built-in browser (online)</a> supports sign-in and keeps browsing work inside ChatGPT without using your regular browser profile.</p> <p>ChatGPT can also switch between tools as a task requires, using plugins when a dedicated integration is available, your browser when it needs signed-in browser context, and the built-in browser for localhost.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Notice（<code>warning</code>）</strong>: Treat page content as untrusted context, and review the website before allowing ChatGPT to continue.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"use-chatgpt-from-chrome\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"use-side-chat-in-your-browser\">Use side chat in your browser</h2> <p>Side chat is available in Chrome, Edge, Brave, and Vivaldi.</p> <p>Open ChatGPT beside the page you're viewing to ask about the page or continue into tasks that can use its context alongside local files and connected apps. ChatGPT can use context from your open tabs when a task needs it.</p> <ol> <li>Open the page you want to work with.</li> <li>Select ChatGPT from the browser toolbar or <strong>Extensions</strong> menu. On macOS, you can also press <kbd>Cmd</kbd>+<kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>.</kbd>.</li> <li>Ask a question about the page or give ChatGPT a task.</li> </ol> <p>The panel stays with the tab where you opened it. Chats you start in side chat are available in the ChatGPT app, and you can open recent ChatGPT chats in the side chat, so you can continue work in either place.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: ChatGPT open beside the current Chrome tab.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"bring-tabs-and-selected-text-into-a-chat\">Bring tabs and selected text into a chat</h2> <p>Mention an open browser tab in the desktop app when you want ChatGPT to use that page as context. In browsers with side chat, you can also mention tabs there, or highlight text on a page and bring the selection into your chat to ask about a specific passage without copying the whole page.</p> <p>In browsers with side chat, you can also right-click the page and select <strong>Ask ChatGPT</strong>. The side chat opens with the relevant page context so you can continue the request in your browser.</p> <h3 id=\"ask-about-a-youtube-video\">Ask about a YouTube video</h3> <p>Open a YouTube video, then ask a question about it in a supported side chat. When captions are available, ChatGPT can use the video's timestamped transcript to explain, summarize, or answer questions about the content.</p> <p>Treat webpage content, selected text, and video transcripts as untrusted context. Review the page and any requested permissions before asking ChatGPT to use or act on that information.</p> <p><a id=\"set-up-the-chrome-extension\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"set-up-your-browser\">Set up your browser</h2> <p>Install the browser on your computer, then open <strong>Settings &gt; Computer Use</strong> in the ChatGPT desktop app. Expand <strong>More browsers</strong> if your browser isn't shown in the main list.</p> <ol> <li>Select your browser and follow any prompt to install the required plugin.</li> <li>Select <strong>Install</strong> beside the browser to open its extension store page. Install the ChatGPT extension and review the browser's permission prompts.</li> <li>Return to <strong>Computer Use</strong> and confirm that the browser shows <strong>Manage</strong>.</li> <li>Start a ChatGPT Work or Codex chat and select your browser with an <code>@</code>-mention. Use the browser profile where you installed the extension.</li> </ol> <p>The browser's toggle in <strong>Computer Use</strong> controls whether it appears in the <code>@</code>-mention menu. Select <strong>Manage</strong> to change website permissions instead.</p> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Computer Use settings showing Google Chrome connected through the Chrome extension.</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-a-chrome-task-from-chatgpt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"start-a-browser-task-from-chatgpt\">Start a browser task from ChatGPT</h2> <p>After setup, start a new ChatGPT Work or Codex chat. Select <strong>Chrome</strong>, <strong>Edge</strong>, <strong>Brave Browser</strong>, <strong>Opera</strong>, or <strong>Vivaldi</strong> from the <code>@</code>-mention menu to choose which browser ChatGPT uses. For example:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">@Edge open Salesforce and update the account from these call notes.\n</code></pre> <p>You can also mention an open tab to give ChatGPT context from that page. Opera supports these desktop workflows even though it doesn't have side chat.</p> <h2 id=\"control-website-access\">Control website access</h2> <p>By default, ChatGPT asks before it interacts with each new website. ChatGPT bases the prompt on the website host, such as <code>example.com</code>.</p> <p>When ChatGPT asks to use a website, you can choose the option that matches the task and your risk tolerance:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Allow once</strong> to let ChatGPT use the website one time.</li> <li><strong>Allow for this site</strong> so ChatGPT can use the website again without asking.</li> <li><strong>Allow for all sites</strong> so ChatGPT can use websites without asking.</li> <li><strong>Decline</strong> to prevent ChatGPT from using the website.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"manage-allowed-and-blocked-websites\">Manage allowed and blocked websites</h3> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, go to <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Computer Use</strong>, then select <strong>Manage</strong> next to your browser to manage an allowlist and blocklist for domains. The allowlist contains domains ChatGPT can use without asking again. The blocklist contains domains ChatGPT shouldn't use. The supported browsers share these website permissions.</p> <p>Removing a domain from the allowlist means ChatGPT asks again before using it. Removing a domain from the blocklist means ChatGPT can ask again instead of treating the domain as blocked.</p> <h4 id=\"allow-for-all-sites\">Allow for all sites</h4> <p>If you select <strong>Allow for all sites</strong>, ChatGPT no longer asks for confirmation before using websites. Only choose this option if you trust ChatGPT to use any website open in the browser.</p> <h4 id=\"browser-history\">Browser history</h4> <p>Browser history can include sensitive telemetry, internal URLs, search terms, and activity from browser sessions on signed-in devices. If you allow ChatGPT to access browser history, relevant history entries can become part of the context ChatGPT uses for the task. Malicious or misleading page content can increase the risk that ChatGPT copies this data somewhere unintended.</p> <p>ChatGPT asks when it wants to use browser history. ChatGPT scopes history access to the request, and history doesn't have an always-allow option.</p> <h2 id=\"data-and-security\">Data and security</h2> <p><a id=\"chrome-extension-permissions\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"browser-extension-permissions\">Browser extension permissions</h3> <p>Your browser asks you to accept permissions when you install the extension. For example, Chrome's permission prompt may include:</p> <ul> <li>Access the page debugger</li> <li>Read and change all your data on all websites</li> <li>Read and change your browsing history on all your signed-in devices</li> <li>Display notifications</li> <li>Read and change your bookmarks</li> <li>Manage your downloads</li> <li>Communicate with cooperating native applications</li> <li>View and manage your tab groups</li> </ul> <p>These extension permissions make it capable of operating browser workflows. ChatGPT still uses its own confirmations, settings, allowlists, and blocklists before using websites or browser history during a task.</p> <h3 id=\"memories\">Memories</h3> <p>Computer Use follows your Memories setting. If Memories is on, ChatGPT can use relevant saved memories while working in your browser. If Memories is off, browser control doesn't use memories.</p> <h3 id=\"what-openai-stores-from-browsing\">What OpenAI stores from browsing</h3> <p>OpenAI doesn't store a separate complete record of your browser actions from the extension. OpenAI stores browser activity only when it becomes part of the ChatGPT context, such as text ChatGPT reads from a page, screenshots, tool calls, summaries, messages, or other content included in the chat.</p> <p>Your ChatGPT data controls apply to content processed in context. Avoid sending secrets or highly sensitive data through browser tasks unless they're required and you are present to review each prompt.</p> <h2 id=\"troubleshooting\">Troubleshooting</h2> <p>If ChatGPT can't connect to your browser, first confirm the website ChatGPT is trying to access isn't in the blocklist in Settings. If the website isn't blocked, work through these checks:</p> <ol> <li>Update the ChatGPT desktop app. If you have more than one ChatGPT or Codex desktop app installed, update each one or remove copies you no longer use.</li> <li>Restart your browser. In Chrome, Edge, Brave, or Vivaldi, reopen ChatGPT from the toolbar or <strong>Extensions</strong> menu and confirm the side chat loads. Opera doesn't have side chat; check its connection from the desktop app.</li> <li>In <strong>Settings &gt; Computer Use</strong>, confirm that your browser appears and shows <strong>Manage</strong>. If it still shows <strong>Install</strong>, follow the setup flow again. Turn on its toggle if the browser is missing from the <code>@</code>-mention menu.</li> <li>Make sure you are using the browser profile where the extension is installed. If you use more than one profile, install and enable the extension in the active profile.</li> <li>Start a new ChatGPT Work or Codex chat and try the browser task again. This can clear chat-specific connection state.</li> <li>Restart the ChatGPT desktop app, then try again. If the extension still doesn't connect, reinstall it through <strong>Settings &gt; Computer Use</strong>.</li> <li>If ChatGPT still can't use the browser, run <code>/feedback</code> in the app and include the chat ID when you contact support.</li> </ol> <h3 id=\"upload-files\">Upload files</h3> <p>If a Chrome task needs to upload a file from your computer, allow the Chrome extension to access file URLs in Chrome:</p> <ol> <li>In Chrome, open the extensions icon in the toolbar, then click <strong>Manage Extensions</strong>.</li> <li>On the extension card, click <strong>Details</strong>.</li> <li>Turn on <strong>Allow access to file URLs</strong>.</li> </ol> <p>After you change the setting, start the Chrome task again.</p>"};
